From: JoinMarket NG <dev@joinmarket-ng.local>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] feat(channelescrowrpc): add exact-parent channel escrow

Add a durable, fail-closed cooperative signer for quiescent simple Taproot
channels. It cosigns only one authorized parent transaction that spends the
channel funding output, returns the channel input witness before broadcast so
the remaining CoinJoin inputs can be signed, and classifies that parent as a
cooperative funding spend.

Signing evidence, the finalized parent and the MuSig2 transcript are persisted
so a client can reconcile after an LND restart. Cancellation is recorded
atomically with the lock release, so an interrupted cancel can be retried
safely and a stale cancel cannot release a newer session. An escrow lock blocks
cooperative renegotiation and abandonment but still allows an explicit force
close with the current commitment.
